From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepGProp by-plane overloads measure
 about the plane the caller passed, not its mirror through the origin

Every by-plane BRepGProp_Vinert and BRepGProp_VinertGK overload re-bases the
plane's fourth coefficient on the location point the same way:

  thePlane.Coefficients(aCoeff[0], aCoeff[1], aCoeff[2], aCoeff[3]);
  aCoeff[3] = aCoeff[3] - aCoeff[0] * loc.X() - aCoeff[1] * loc.Y() - aCoeff[2] * loc.Z();

and both integrands then subtract that coefficient rather than adding it.
BRepGProp_Gauss::computeVInertiaOfElementaryPart (BRepGProp_Gauss.cxx:343):

  double d1 = theCoeff[0] * x + theCoeff[1] * y + theCoeff[2] * z - theCoeff[3];

and BRepGProp_UFunction::VolumeValue (BRepGProp_UFunction.cxx:99), which the
Gauss-Kronrod path uses:

  theD1 = thePMP0.X() * aCoeff[0] + thePMP0.Y() * aCoeff[1] + thePMP0.Z() * aCoeff[2] - aCoeff[3];

In both, x, y, z (thePMP0) is P - loc. gp_Pln::Coefficients gives a, b, c, d for
a x + b y + c z + d = 0, so the signed distance from the plane to P is n . P + d.
Substituting the stored coefficient gives

  d1 = n . (P - loc) - (d - n . loc) = n . P - d

which is the signed distance to the plane at n . X == d, the reflection of the
caller's plane through the origin. Both halves of the stored line are wrong in
the same direction: the offset carries the wrong sign, and loc cancels out of
the result entirely rather than re-basing it, so SetLocation has no effect on a
by-plane computation at all.

Negating the coefficient as it is stored fixes both halves at once. With
aCoeff[3] = -d - n . loc the integrands compute

  d1 = n . (P - loc) + d + n . loc = n . P + d

which is the signed distance to the plane as passed, and is independent of loc,
as a distance to a plane must be. The integrands are left alone: their minus
sign is what makes loc re-base correctly once the stored offset has the right
sign, and changing them instead would need the same edit at these five sites
anyway.

Measured on macOS arm64 against the v4.0.0-kernel.3 asset by
Scripts/repro/2827/probe.mm's reportSignConvention, on a flat cap of area
371.7256661 square to the plane normal, where mass == (n . n_face) * area * d1
exactly, so mass / area reads d1 off directly. The cap is at z = 2:

  loc.z  plane at z =   mass              d1     geometric distance
  0      0              743.45133223538    2      2
  0      1             1115.1769983531     3      1
  0      -100         -36429.115279534   -98    102
  3      0              743.45133223538    2      2
  3      1             1115.1769983531     3      1
  3      -100         -36429.115279534   -98    102

d1 tracks z + planeOffset where it should track z - planeOffset, and loc changes
nothing. Both are what the derivation above predicts.

Aggregates do not change. d1 stays an affine function of P with gradient n,
which is the only property the divergence-theorem identities need, so the
per-face sum over a closed shell is still the enclosed volume and the
mass-weighted sum of the per-face centres is still the first moment, for any
plane. BRepGProp::VolumePropertiesGK(S, Props, thePln, ...) therefore reports
the same volume and centre of mass before and after. What changes is a per-face
reading, which is the decomposition a caller asks for when it passes a plane
rather than a point.

All five by-plane sites are in this change, because they are one convention
rather than five defects: BRepGProp_Vinert.cxx:280, :297 and :314, covering the
four Perform(gp_Pln) overloads and the Gauss integrand, and
BRepGProp_VinertGK.cxx:219 and :244, covering the two Perform(gp_Pln) overloads
and the Gauss-Kronrod integrand. Fixing one class and not the other would leave
BRepGProp::VolumeProperties and BRepGProp::VolumePropertiesGK disagreeing per
face about which plane they measured.

Nothing in OCCT reads a per-face by-plane value, so nothing in OCCT depends on
the old convention: BRepGProp.cxx:311 is the only BRepGProp_Vinert call site and
passes a point, and BRepGProp.cxx:809 and :892 forward a plane to
BRepGProp_VinertGK for an aggregate, which this does not change. Until carried
patch 0043 the by-plane mass was overwritten with 0.0 before any caller could
see it, so the value this corrects has never been readable from a release build.

SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#2873.
---
